    return copy;
}
// Zetsu shows every app as its full-screen picture scaled into the window (per axis: a tiled, narrow window squashed the app to half its width).
// "Flex": the app is laid out at the window's own content size instead, like Aerial does, and shown 1:1. Zetsu keeps sending the app a full-screen
// frame; while a window is flexed those updates carry the window's content frame instead (gZetsuFlexFrames, bundle -> on-screen content rect).
